WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:04.710
Ivan: There’s a very famous saying that
any advanced technology becomes indistinguishable

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:05.710
from magic.

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:09.780
That’s one of the things we talked about
with Soli it’s a sort of magical sensor.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.260
Baratunde: I did it!

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.050
I touched without touching!

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:19.060
Jamie: Radar has a lot of very interesting
properties that would be very useful for human

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:20.289
computer interaction.

00:00:20.289 --> 00:00:21.289
You can shrink it down.

00:00:21.289 --> 00:00:22.779
B: All of this is now in there?

00:00:22.779 --> 00:00:23.779
Jamie: That’s right, yeah.

00:00:23.779 --> 00:00:27.300
It can sense through materials, it’s extremely
sensitive for motion.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:32.320
Leo: So we built this new interaction paradigm
based on the understanding of body language,

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:33.859
distances, and gestures.

00:00:33.859 --> 00:00:38.809
Ivan: How can we make a language interaction
with technology closer to what we do naturally

00:00:38.809 --> 00:00:39.809
in the real world.

00:00:39.809 --> 00:00:43.590
Leo: Then of course, we really need to test
to distinguish between intentional and unintentional

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:44.590
gestures.

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:45.940
Just because I wave on top of the device...

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:46.940
Baratunde: Yes

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:47.940
Leo: Doesn’t mean I want to skip a song.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:52.530
Leo: If I pick up coffee cup, this gesture
is very similar to a swipe, and this is really

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:53.530
important.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:54.530
Baratunde: Ok

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:55.530
Leo: And then I can do this

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:56.530
Baratunde: Whoa

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:57.530
Leo: And it actually works

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:58.530
Baratunde: Hmmm

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:01.379
Leo: With Soli we can try to understand more
about the implicit behavior that happens around

00:01:01.379 --> 00:01:02.379
the device.

00:01:02.379 --> 00:01:04.440
Baratunde: The phone knows earlier what your
intention is.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:05.440
Leo: Exactly.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:06.570
Let’s say the alarm goes off.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:07.570
SFX: Phone beeping

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:08.570
Leo: Really annoying.

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:09.570
Baratunde: Yep

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:10.570
Leo: As you reach, we can lower the volume.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:11.570
Baratunde: Ahhhh

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:12.570
Leo: The phone is more polite.

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:14.530
And then you can just go gesture to shut it
off.

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:15.530
Baratunde: Laughing

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:19.310
Leo: This moment of understanding each other
happens all the time between us.

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:20.770
But it never happened with technology.

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:25.899
What we can do with radar is to actually capture
aspects of non-verbal communication.

00:01:25.899 --> 00:01:30.210
And as a first step with Pixel 4 with Motion
Sense is to get as close as possible to the

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.369
intuitiveness of verbal interaction.

00:01:32.369 --> 00:01:33.450
Baratunde: Silence!

